WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.356 --> 00:00:03.640
Today we have a very special guest.

2
00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:07.120
All three seasons of her series, Odd Mom Out,

3
00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:09.760
just dropped on Peacock.

4
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.400
Well, she's always my dear friend

5
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.400
and my children's aunt

6
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.360
and one of the most important people in my life.

7
00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:16.461
It's actress and comedian, Jill Kargman.

8
00:00:16.461 --> 00:00:18.040
(applause)

9
00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:19.503
Thank you.
I love you.

10
00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:24.020
Okay, so we're gonna do some Thanksgiving

11
00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.710
based new stories.
Great.

12
00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:26.930
Based.

13
00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:27.763
Basted.

14
00:00:27.763 --> 00:00:29.590
I see what you did there.

15
00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:30.423
Okay.

16
00:00:30.423 --> 00:00:34.020
Across the country, many first time turkey cooks

17
00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:37.619
are tackling their very first bird.

18
00:00:37.619 --> 00:00:40.140
(mock turkey gobbling)

19
00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.850
And wow, there is a lot of messing up going around.

20
00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:45.690
Did I thaw that enough?

21
00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:47.410
When do I bast?

22
00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:49.400
Did I get all the goop out

23
00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.261
or did I leave some goop in?

24
00:00:51.261 --> 00:00:54.210
(goofy warbling)

25
00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:56.680
So, CNN reports that Whole Foods

26
00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.840
has teamed up with Progressive

27
00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.060
to offer turkey insurance this year.

28
00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:03.390
It's like.

29
00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:04.340
These two companies were like,

30
00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:05.983 line:15%
what's one thing we can control?

31
00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:08.640 line:15%
If you bought a Whole Foods bird

32
00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:10.050 line:15%
and suffer a turkey fail,

33
00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:13.090 line:15%
you can get a $35 Whole Food gift card back

34
00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:14.940 line:15%
all you have to do is send in the receipt

35
00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:17.743 line:15%
and a photo and description of your terrible turkey.

36
00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:21.020
Jill, what are you doing for Thanksgiving?

37
00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:22.670
I'm supporting local restaurants

38
00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:25.053
by ordering everything and cooking nothing.

39
00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:28.690
But we're all getting a Turkey Day surprise this week

40
00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:29.783
from Zoom.

41
00:01:29.783 --> 00:01:32.960
CNET reports Zoom is lifting their 40 minute limit

42
00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:34.770
on calls all day long Thursday.

43
00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:37.290
So if you're planning to use the 40 minute limit

44
00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:38.946
as an excuse to keep it short.

45
00:01:38.946 --> 00:01:40.803
Time to find another excuse.

46
00:01:40.803 --> 00:01:42.010
(audience laughing)

47
00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:43.860 line:15%
Yeah, that's awkward.

48
00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:45.261 line:15%
Blame it on the bladder.

49
00:01:45.261 --> 00:01:46.330 line:15%
(audience laughing)

50
00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:47.490 line:15%
Gotta go.

51
00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:48.590 line:15%
Well, okay.

52
00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:51.710 line:15%
So if your turkey goes wrong, you got insurance.

53
00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:53.610
If you want to avoid your family,

54
00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:55.020
now there's no excuses.

55
00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:55.853
Next.

56
00:01:55.853 --> 00:01:57.990
It's been the most challenging year

57
00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:01.690
but people around the country are still giving back

58
00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:04.700
and I love this story so much from Kansas.

59
00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:07.283
A barber named Nate Rivera

60
00:02:07.283 --> 00:02:10.400
is offering haircuts for Turkeys

61
00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.600 line:15%
for the second year in a row.

62
00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:16.060 line:15%
Donate a turkey, get a free haircut.

63
00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:17.240 line:15%
And this years different though.

64
00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:19.520 line:15%
Covid has shut down his barber shop

65
00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:20.930 line:15%
but Nate and his wife, Erica,

66
00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:23.220 line:15%
are still collecting turkeys and sides

67
00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:25.190 line:15%
for their families who need them

68
00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:27.590 line:15%
and in return, Nate's offering a voucher,

69
00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:31.336 line:15%
a promise for a haircut when his shops reopens.

70
00:02:31.336 --> 00:02:32.169
(applause)

71
00:02:32.169 --> 00:02:34.500
Stories like this, they really inspire me

72
00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:37.670
and they're exactly what I wanted to do this program for

73
00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:40.800 line:15%
and if you're looking for more ways to donate this season,

74
00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:41.960 line:15%
go to our website.

75
00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:44.350 line:15%
We've got some great ways to give back.

76
00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:46.240
All right, and finally.

77
00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.360
Jill, you actually brought something.

78
00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:49.448
I did.

79
00:02:49.448 --> 00:02:53.040
So I wanted to get you a traditional Thanksgiving dessert

80
00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:57.130
to enjoy and this looks like a normal cake

81
00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:59.750
but I would say why stop at one dessert

82
00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:02.180
when you can have many?

83
00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:05.200
So introducing, everybody, the Piecakein.

84
00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:08.140 line:15%
It's the Turducken of Thanksgiving sweets.

85
00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:09.343 line:15%
If you lift your cloche.

86
00:03:10.457 --> 00:03:12.060 line:15%
This is a cloche!

87
00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:12.910
It is a cloche.

88
00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.560
It's part pecan pie in a pumpkin pie

89
00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.870
in a spice cake with apple pie filling

90
00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:20.940
all in cinnamon butter crumb

91
00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:23.110
with some o'crumble up on it.

92
00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:24.611
Oh my.

93
00:03:24.611 --> 00:03:25.540
(applause)

94
00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:28.320
I want to get everything all in one bite,

95
00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:29.803
the way nature intended.

96
00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:34.000
It's much better than a Turducken.

97
00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:34.833
Oh my god.

98
00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:38.970
Sweets on sweets are better than meats on meats.

99
00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:42.131
Oh my gosh!

100
00:03:42.131 --> 00:03:42.964
That is so good.

101
00:03:42.964 --> 00:03:45.130
Usually on shows, I see people eating garbage

102
00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:46.970
and I'm like, how do they force feed that?

103
00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:48.929
But I'm genuinely inhaling this.

104
00:03:48.929 --> 00:03:50.390
(audience laughing)

105
00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:52.487
I just want to thank Jill.

106
00:03:52.487 --> 00:03:53.424
I love you.

107
00:03:53.424 --> 00:03:55.587
You have a whole other Piecakein on deck.

108
00:03:55.587 --> 00:03:56.420
(audience laughing)

109
00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:58.010
And I just want to say something.

110
00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:03.010
As a cast member myself on Odd Mom Out.

111
00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:04.960
Yes, you were so good.

112
00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:06.570
It was the best time ever

113
00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:08.660
and I love this show so much.

114
00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:10.380
I loved being a part of it

115
00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:12.200
and I really loved watching it.

116
00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:13.033
So nice.

117
00:04:13.033 --> 00:04:13.866
Well, I love you.
Love you.

118
00:04:13.866 --> 00:04:15.524
And to everyone out there,

119
00:04:15.524 --> 00:04:19.768
eat, enjoy, be happy, be healthy, be safe.

120
00:04:19.768 --> 00:04:22.435
(upbeat music)

